 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Support
+
+Metrics can be gated with optional thresholds to enable CI/CD automation. The `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option gates on metric scores:
+- `frai eval --outputs out.json --references ref.json --threshold exact_match=0.9`
+- Multiple thresholds: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`
+- Exits 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 on validation error (malformed threshold, unknown metric).
+- Reports always generated before exit code is applied.
+- JSON and Markdown reports include `passed: boolean` and a `thresholds` array when thresholds are specified.
+- Metrics with no score (e.g., `exact_match` without references) fail their threshold.
+- SDK users: `generateReport({evaluations, thresholds: {exact_match: 0.9}})` adds same fields.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
